WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.944
Every computer, from a phone to a laptop, does the same four things.

2
00:00:04.294 --> 00:00:08.830
It takes input, it processes it, it shows output, and it stores what matters.

3
00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.644
Let's follow one small sum, two plus three, all the way through.

4
00:00:13.844 --> 00:00:15.180
First, input.

5
00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.874
You press the keys two, plus, and three.

6
00:00:18.224 --> 00:00:22.760
Each key press becomes an electrical signal that travels into the computer.

7
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.496
Inside the computer, everything is a number.

8
00:00:26.846 --> 00:00:29.654
The character two is stored as the number fifty.

9
00:00:30.004 --> 00:00:36.460
In binary, that is zero zero one one zero zero one zero: eight tiny on and off switches called bits.

10
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:41.444
These numbers are kept in RAM, the computer's short-term memory.

11
00:00:41.794 --> 00:00:44.922
Picture RAM as a long row of numbered lockers.

12
00:00:45.272 --> 00:00:48.512
Our sum, two plus three, waits in locker zero five.

13
00:00:49.712 --> 00:00:52.840
Now the CPU, the brain of the computer, gets to work.

14
00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.566
It fetches the instruction from the locker.

15
00:00:55.916 --> 00:01:00.052
It decodes it, which means working out what it asks for: add two and three.

16
00:01:00.402 --> 00:01:03.610
Then it executes it, and the answer is five.

17
00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.712
A CPU repeats this cycle billions of times every second.

18
00:01:08.912 --> 00:01:12.040
The answer goes back into memory, and then to the screen.

19
00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:14.510
Seeing the five appear is the output.

20
00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:17.094
There is one catch.

21
00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:20.524
RAM forgets everything the moment the power goes off.

22
00:01:20.874 --> 00:01:27.186
So when you save, the computer copies your work to storage, such as an SSD, which remembers it even without power.

23
00:01:28.386 --> 00:01:30.266
So, input goes in.

24
00:01:30.616 --> 00:01:33.600
The CPU processes it, using memory.

25
00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:35.398
Output comes out.

26
00:01:35.748 --> 00:01:37.916
And storage keeps your work safe.

27
00:01:38.266 --> 00:01:40.162
That is how every computer works.
